  "description": "QOTSAX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H88 Dy6 N12 O31,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.559-4.023 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.93-115.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C76H88Dy6N12O31·2(C2H3N). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
